What Are Landing Gear Overhaul Services?
Landing gear overhaul services involve comprehensive inspection, maintenance, repair, and restoration of aircraft landing gear systems. These systems support an aircraft during ground operations, absorb landing forces, and enable safe taxiing and takeoff.

An overhaul may include disassembly, cleaning, nondestructive testing, structural inspections, replacement of worn components, corrosion treatment, reassembly, and functional testing. The precise scope depends on aircraft type, operating history, maintenance requirements, and applicable aviation regulations.

The market encompasses overhaul parts, specialized service packages, and supporting technologies used by aircraft manufacturers, airlines, independent MRO organizations, and military aviation operators.

Key Market Drivers
1. Expansion of Commercial Aircraft Fleets
Growing air travel and airline fleet expansion increase demand for scheduled aircraft maintenance. As aircraft accumulate flight hours and landing cycles, landing gear components require inspection and servicing to maintain safe operation.

Airlines also seek to extend the useful life of existing aircraft while balancing maintenance expenses against the cost of purchasing replacements. These priorities support demand for qualified overhaul providers with reliable repair capabilities and efficient turnaround times.

2. Stringent Aviation Safety and Maintenance Requirements
Aviation authorities require operators to maintain aircraft in an airworthy condition through approved inspection and maintenance procedures. Landing gear overhaul is an important part of this process because component wear, corrosion, and mechanical damage can affect aircraft safety.

Compliance requirements create recurring demand for specialized service providers capable of meeting technical documentation, quality assurance, certification, and traceability requirements.

3. Adoption of Digital and Predictive Maintenance Technologies
Digital inspection systems, advanced diagnostics, and predictive analytics are creating opportunities to improve overhaul planning. These tools can help technicians identify component issues, organize maintenance workflows, and improve the use of workshop resources.

Digital twins and automated inspection methods may also support more consistent evaluation of components, helping MRO providers improve operational efficiency and service quality.

